This paper studies stochastic contextual bandits with knapsacks (CBwK) in the small budget regime where the initial budget $B = \Omega(\sqrt{T})$. The authors propose the Adaptive and Universal Primal--Dual (AUPD) algorithm, which achieves $	ilde{O}((1 +  rac{
u^*}{\delta b})\sqrt{T})$ regret under the strict feasibility assumption without requiring prior knowledge of the feasibility margin, matching the best-known bounds. Under the more general setting without strict feasibility, AUPD achieves the first known regret bound of $	ilde{O}(\sqrt{T} +  rac{
u^*}{\sqrt{b}}T^{ rac{3}{4}})$, which is significant given the lack of prior results in this regime. The algorithm uses a novel budget-aware design with a virtual queue mechanism and Lyapunov drift analysis to balance reward maximization and budget consumption.

